{"name":"Yellow Trumpet","hex":"#f9d988","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"yellow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of sunflower petals and lemons; the color obtained by mixing green and red light, or by subtracting blue from white light; the color evoked by light of wavelength around 580 nm; one of the three primary colors in subtractive color systems.","The middle light in a set of three traffic lights, the lighting of which indicates that drivers should stop short of the intersection if it is safe to do so."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a yellow hue.","Lacking courage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yellow"},{"term":"trumpet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A musical instrument of the brass family, generally tuned to the key of B-flat; by extension, any type of lip-vibrated aerophone, most often valveless and not chromatic.","Someone who plays the trumpet; a trumpeter."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To sound loudly, be amplified","To play the trumpet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trumpet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Costus spectabilis","blocks":[{"text":"Costus spectabilis, commonly known as the yellow trumpet, or yellow bell, is an African species of herb; low and perennial, it is found from Sierra Leone to Sudan to as far south as Angola and Zimbabwe."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Costus_spectabilis00%2C_white_background.jpg/330px-Costus_spectabilis00%2C_white_background.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Costus_spectabilis"},{"title":"Trumpet","blocks":[{"text":"The trumpet is a brass instrument. The most common type of trumpet is a transposing instrument in B♭, with pitches sounding a whole step lower than written. The trumpet family includes instruments ranging from the piccolo trumpet, with the highest register in the brass family, to the bass trumpet, pitched one octave below the standard B♭ or C trumpet."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Yamaha_Trumpet_YTR-8335LA_crop.jpg/330px-Yamaha_Trumpet_YTR-8335LA_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trumpet"},{"title":"Yellow","blocks":[{"text":"Yellow is a color between green and orange on the spectrum of light. It is evoked by light with a dominant wavelength of roughly 575–585 nm. It is a primary color in subtractive color systems, used in painting or color printing. In the RGB color model, used to create colors on television and computer screens, yellow is a secondary color made by combining red and green at equal intensity. Carotenoids give the characteristic yellow color to autumn leaves, corn, canaries, daffodils, and lemons, as well as egg yolks, buttercups, and bananas. They absorb light energy and protect plants from photo damage in some cases. Sunlight has a slight yellowish hue when the Sun is near the horizon, due to atmospheric scattering of shorter wavelengths."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg/330px-Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Musicians_at_the_coal_yard_-_DPLA_-_654d5920548ca26c571a5337d7807c60.jpg/500px-Musicians_at_the_coal_yard_-_DPLA_-_654d5920548ca26c571a5337d7807c60.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Musicians_at_the_coal_yard_-_DPLA_-_654d5920548ca26c571a5337d7807c60.jpg/500px-Musicians_at_the_coal_yard_-_DPLA_-_654d5920548ca26c571a5337d7807c60.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Trio of trumpeters in Toledo, Ohio, approximately